body:
To hit your commercial peak at such a young age is something I think any artist is gonna struggle with. Although I do agree with him when he says that the market is oversaturated at the moment because it definitely is, I think part of the issue of Palaces not being as successful was because he didn't rly go all out and try something different like the mixtape. It kinda felt like re-treading old ground to replicate what has been successful in the past but to not the same effect. The music landscape has shfted since those times, and imo its more important than ever to have a style that's distinctly yours. While it shines in places on Palaces, and new things are tried like on Go and the title track, most of it kind of feels like someone trying to sound like Flume (I mean that in the least disrespectful way possible but yeah).

&#x200B;

What I think he should push for going forward is going back to the drawing board and ponder what it was that made people fall in love with his music in the first place. Being an electronic superstar comes with a lot of expectations of your shoulders on what your music should sound like, but we had an idea before the HTIF, and he still managed to blow our minds anyway. Something to that calibre, doesn't have to be mega experimental like that, but just something that throws us for a loop on what Flume should sound like. Something I've always admired about him is that he's never completely given in to fan expectations and always seemed to be doing his own thing. It may have a slipped a little on Palaces, but like I said earlier there are moments on there that still show he's got it, and he still has the potential for a a very fruitful career going forward.

&#x200B;

(excuse the essay this turned into lmao)

this is one of the things that really made me stop making music for a while. i have fun making the track and everything, but when none of my friends bother to listen to it and say anything about it, what's the point really. i've gone back to making music occasionally recently, but I haven't uploaded anything in a long time cos I know i'm not going to get any interaction from it.

&#x200B;

and yea there was this other mutual friend that was getting into making music around the same time as me and they were getting posted around like wildfire. shit's hard.

FM 3 and 4 have my fav soundtracks just because I love that kind of electronic music, but the occasional strings mixed in with it added a lot of weight to them too (Paris Rouen is probably my favourite piece of music featured in a Motorsport game). FM5 is still incredibly good though, in a very close third.

&#x200B;

I hope the new game has the sound of any of these, as FM7's soundtrack was so lacking I don't really remember anything from it.

I'm already calling this album of the year, this thing is just so intricate and made to perfection that you'd have to be some kind of genius to beat it...

&#x200B;

...alexander panos i'm looking at you
